[{:db/id "q-71250/selection/26036640a5a568cf8e17040251fffebee138e92b8d84929ad3940154dcad7346" :answer/id #uuid "3d480cf1-d8da-52d8-acad-12613d2abecb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,2,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71250/selection/ce820b2de3a32f02825ff682c2e6b565f1282a7bd39ec3f734095df537fc23ea" :answer/id #uuid "bb462a2a-a8ea-5c52-87e2-5ce0a4b58c30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2,3,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71250/selection/b4230d38a0d3aa35ba6f8d9d6f71c8298e3591392aaf4c3d65617b3b49a069db" :answer/id #uuid "d3305f30-d7c9-5c02-bade-e779c12955d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,2,-5⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71250/selection/d1927dd8f2c05c02673da81e86db8a6bc9303a450ff810a343f9d65837258578" :answer/id #uuid "0015dfe6-66b1-5bcb-b770-6499254a0c7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,0,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71250/selection/6f405fd4a764836bce0df6e3b438c7f87f905d91227bc8c7d6cb65fd3a36beaf" :answer/id #uuid "f346f7d9-30ff-5b4b-8f11-4c0d3f6de38f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,1,-3⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71250/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "86e9dc10-4419-568e-b48f-c804abae583a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71250/selection/ce820b2de3a32f02825ff682c2e6b565f1282a7bd39ec3f734095df537fc23ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-71250/selection/26036640a5a568cf8e17040251fffebee138e92b8d84929ad3940154dcad7346" "q-71250/selection/ce820b2de3a32f02825ff682c2e6b565f1282a7bd39ec3f734095df537fc23ea" "q-71250/selection/b4230d38a0d3aa35ba6f8d9d6f71c8298e3591392aaf4c3d65617b3b49a069db" "q-71250/selection/d1927dd8f2c05c02673da81e86db8a6bc9303a450ff810a343f9d65837258578" "q-71250/selection/6f405fd4a764836bce0df6e3b438c7f87f905d91227bc8c7d6cb65fd3a36beaf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71250" :question/id #uuid "a2b8a634-f438-5018-bd9b-7ab535d7a931" :question/math-academy-id "q-71250" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-x+z-3=0 \\\\ 3x+2y-5=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $-x+z-3=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨-1,0,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $3x+2y-5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨3,2,0⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,1⟩\\times ⟨3,2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-2i+3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,3,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71250/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71250"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129174/selection/98bdbe15356386d14a6cd7c61c6be42bfc55962f7348e86cae7962ed5f29a898" :answer/id #uuid "1f8173bc-fe42-5904-8df7-f78bca46ebc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,-2,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129174/selection/ac554f30ea956a391ac0db5db4005a8c6e837ce1e390a57f43d7409be2e6763d" :answer/id #uuid "6b74c54b-4ee2-55ae-bb61-e9f201dea629" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2,2,0⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129174/selection/ce1ca562372fc238d110a3f9dbd5b8cfbab74a31e73499812ed5036b9225e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "2c096c0e-c190-5f6b-8899-78d8a134d8b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,-2,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129174/selection/98291c34e10d36533aa1cade7ff257b84607330b87736c5344af305614416f71" :answer/id #uuid "8d727482-e328-5e27-9509-1c4960039de1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2,1,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129174/selection/94a921968b8f5a5cd789be5290718cdd4c45ebca46c94885b60c2ca764144f67" :answer/id #uuid "6aa606c2-8f2f-5b98-a400-94496b674cc7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,-2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129174/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90eb342c-9408-5539-a9e2-bbb96bd2c38d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129174/selection/98bdbe15356386d14a6cd7c61c6be42bfc55962f7348e86cae7962ed5f29a898" :answer-field/choices ["q-129174/selection/98bdbe15356386d14a6cd7c61c6be42bfc55962f7348e86cae7962ed5f29a898" "q-129174/selection/ac554f30ea956a391ac0db5db4005a8c6e837ce1e390a57f43d7409be2e6763d" "q-129174/selection/ce1ca562372fc238d110a3f9dbd5b8cfbab74a31e73499812ed5036b9225e8e6" "q-129174/selection/98291c34e10d36533aa1cade7ff257b84607330b87736c5344af305614416f71" "q-129174/selection/94a921968b8f5a5cd789be5290718cdd4c45ebca46c94885b60c2ca764144f67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129174" :question/id #uuid "c61ebc2f-8bbc-5c89-bcf3-6676fa54cd9f" :question/math-academy-id "q-129174" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the planes $2x=6$ and $z=1-y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $2x=6$, a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=1-y$ (or $y+z=1$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129174/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129174"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129168/selection/95734663ea3fab88b9e0d48cac1a88b1f7dce51d987dfd058c96ff94e944abe4" :answer/id #uuid "441a94a3-44b2-5c48-8c6e-0343e4de510b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-2,3,10⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129168/selection/8c2881c7ea2e3f95d00b11dc74813c950f8baba0224cb26bcf1d0786e6b5b5d9" :answer/id #uuid "d8514cc6-e956-570e-8f44-ecbf1cc2b777" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-3,3,10⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129168/selection/6f4d8dc210419d30777910be2280a229d9f64f485e5c208b3718e8f785ce1868" :answer/id #uuid "98700330-3eeb-585a-9203-09b9d81b7eec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨3,-2,-10⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129168/selection/babcbef190a43ea25cf01fc38ac989022440be673eddf059ba9876a7fd60af60" :answer/id #uuid "6615e915-8179-5315-922e-37a674edda05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,3,-10⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129168/selection/875d1b9d8e1b5babc10a30217be9792407b11babf7eb9cd84187e0f736928f6a" :answer/id #uuid "e0ebb07e-8e9e-59a2-a0e3-ff47873117ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,2,-10⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129168/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c3957011-6333-58ef-b929-20d4ad2bfacb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129168/selection/6f4d8dc210419d30777910be2280a229d9f64f485e5c208b3718e8f785ce1868" :answer-field/choices ["q-129168/selection/95734663ea3fab88b9e0d48cac1a88b1f7dce51d987dfd058c96ff94e944abe4" "q-129168/selection/8c2881c7ea2e3f95d00b11dc74813c950f8baba0224cb26bcf1d0786e6b5b5d9" "q-129168/selection/6f4d8dc210419d30777910be2280a229d9f64f485e5c208b3718e8f785ce1868" "q-129168/selection/babcbef190a43ea25cf01fc38ac989022440be673eddf059ba9876a7fd60af60" "q-129168/selection/875d1b9d8e1b5babc10a30217be9792407b11babf7eb9cd84187e0f736928f6a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129168" :question/id #uuid "4ef457fa-f69c-5609-9dab-19d4b3fa6e77" :question/math-academy-id "q-129168" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+3y+10=0 \\\\ 2x-2y+z+15=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $2x+3y+10=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,3,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x-2y+z+15=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,-2,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,3,0⟩\\times ⟨2,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =3i-2j-10k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,-10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129168/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129168"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129171/selection/e655633106092e9b3fc389a7c2d73de16dd514f30108078892d49cf84991f94e" :answer/id #uuid "eb1c5069-f046-5309-89ea-44e56594cba5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨0,6,4⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129171/selection/7f7590780c3080158dd2d56e047d1893a18416180fb9d9287e42a599b0654c35" :answer/id #uuid "ea7b81ed-fe49-5012-a746-8fdb81c47ed8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4,15,10⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129171/selection/d923225480e36ff590185f9ea3cfdd874fbe21adc2bce6b50e5cdff354e2b97c" :answer/id #uuid "7d391d1d-691a-5e30-b1d2-9fc99666d1cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨15,4,10⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129171/selection/ff9957929104c90f6338e4adc7305c01b052b884a88164186830c62a58a7c653" :answer/id #uuid "1e236c63-96bd-5392-ac50-c396ac069c08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨14,11,10⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129171/selection/0c1ec251e3d0307f09c3fb63cc06a36984f71af7287f7c139c192cce08fa66bf" :answer/id #uuid "4c29b290-a959-518e-a935-e2a5adfd783c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨4,0,10⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129171/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f5d7480c-337b-5f49-b755-cc8e97dbac56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129171/selection/7f7590780c3080158dd2d56e047d1893a18416180fb9d9287e42a599b0654c35" :answer-field/choices ["q-129171/selection/e655633106092e9b3fc389a7c2d73de16dd514f30108078892d49cf84991f94e" "q-129171/selection/7f7590780c3080158dd2d56e047d1893a18416180fb9d9287e42a599b0654c35" "q-129171/selection/d923225480e36ff590185f9ea3cfdd874fbe21adc2bce6b50e5cdff354e2b97c" "q-129171/selection/ff9957929104c90f6338e4adc7305c01b052b884a88164186830c62a58a7c653" "q-129171/selection/0c1ec251e3d0307f09c3fb63cc06a36984f71af7287f7c139c192cce08fa66bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129171" :question/id #uuid "85fcd4d1-25d1-559e-b810-7404c2aacc48" :question/math-academy-id "q-129171" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-2z+13=0 \\\\ 2y-3z-25=0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $5x-2z+13=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨5,0,-2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2y-3z-25=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,2,-3⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨5,0,-2⟩\\times ⟨0,2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+15j+10k \\\\  & =⟨4,15,10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129171/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129171"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129175/selection/abd40f1c8abb3b9b6a2b5bd0ce4751316ba547a249a41bced4040c61a906a94b" :answer/id #uuid "f55f11b7-a375-59e4-911f-8491fbf63110" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-3,\\,b=⟨-1,-2,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129175/selection/95ecbe4208a21084d56f58367c8756e57880a55d60f0c65494919f1acad04f5d" :answer/id #uuid "dd366cf3-fab8-5d0f-85e1-0e620a8ac49e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=6,\\,b=⟨-2,2,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129175/selection/47cf3e41b50b4f92d211fc2b05acbfa770f7b99b9d9be11880b94d227f90fdf7" :answer/id #uuid "5ad1c351-8b33-5d91-a19c-839b8f93b72a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-6,\\,b=⟨-2,1,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129175/selection/f92a006b60fd9343a7964d7d3b7d1c5e7d626933205e13a6df35def3a7d8cbad" :answer/id #uuid "e7f37ed3-8b77-55d0-8ce2-ddaf10e71430" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=3,\\,b=⟨-1,2,-2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129175/selection/a9ad6dff29115bd5a1b74cb56130adbed02c3c413cf820ce6a92ec63a10b9605" :answer/id #uuid "03fd85c5-04f3-5b3c-9bee-16cfefcd9514" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=-9,\\,b=⟨2,-2,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129175/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c049a225-10f3-5691-ab8f-07354ee48ff3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129175/selection/abd40f1c8abb3b9b6a2b5bd0ce4751316ba547a249a41bced4040c61a906a94b" :answer-field/choices ["q-129175/selection/abd40f1c8abb3b9b6a2b5bd0ce4751316ba547a249a41bced4040c61a906a94b" "q-129175/selection/95ecbe4208a21084d56f58367c8756e57880a55d60f0c65494919f1acad04f5d" "q-129175/selection/47cf3e41b50b4f92d211fc2b05acbfa770f7b99b9d9be11880b94d227f90fdf7" "q-129175/selection/f92a006b60fd9343a7964d7d3b7d1c5e7d626933205e13a6df35def3a7d8cbad" "q-129175/selection/a9ad6dff29115bd5a1b74cb56130adbed02c3c413cf820ce6a92ec63a10b9605"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129175" :question/id #uuid "8ab147de-05e3-575b-9736-166ad337abc3" :question/math-academy-id "q-129175" :question/problem "The intersection of the planes $2x-y-6=0$ and $y+z+6=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},0,{a}_{3}⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $y=0.$ Substituting this to the first equation gives\n\n$$\n2x-0-6=0\\,⟹\\,x=3,\n$$\n\nand substituting $y=0$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n0+z+6=0\\,⟹\\,z=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=⟨3,0,-6⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $2x-y-6=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,-1,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $y+z+6=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,1,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,0⟩\\times ⟨0,1,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i-2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨3,0,-6⟩+t⟨-1,-2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{3}=3-6=-3,$ and $b=⟨-1,-2,2⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129175/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0302bad-e981-5aee-a70f-66045e7f798a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129175"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129240/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "3e16dced-6a5b-5620-be58-2deed5be94f7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129240/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "bff585ed-0087-519d-b065-55be030055fd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129240/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ed16028f-62c9-50d5-9e6a-84ba0c43acf0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129240/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "d7885c75-9a6b-558b-815a-f3d7f8911130" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129240/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "fba97427-7bd6-5b14-a709-fcfc4f4312a3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129240/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5997ec00-78cd-53e3-b6c1-d68d75c28537" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129240/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-129240/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-129240/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-129240/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-129240/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-129240/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129240" :question/id #uuid "ec4b7b58-5e99-5775-a247-d485bccefd9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129240" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x-y+2z=0$ and $9x-3y+6z+5=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- The planes are parallel but not coincident.\n- The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x-y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,-1,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $9x-3y+6z+5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨9,-3,6⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, ${n}_{2}=3{n}_{1}.$ So, the normal vectors are parallel.\n\n- Statement II is true, while statement III is false. \n\nFor the two planes to coincide, the equation of one plane should be a scalar multiple of the other. However, if we try to manipulate the equation of the second plane to resemble the equation of the first plane, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x-3y+6z+5=0 \\\\ 3x-y+2z+\\frac{5}{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nClearly, this equation is not the same as the equation of the first plane. So, the planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-129240/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129240"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
